        "/^repo='rtree/oshikatsu'; milestone='M0: Feasibility gates'\nissue_a=\\$\\(gh issue create --repo \"\\$repo\" --title 'Gate 0-A: Prove World v4 ballot signal binding' --label spike --label protocol --label world-id --label evidence --milestone \"\\$milestone\" --body \\$'## Outcome\\\\nA production World ID v4 Proof of Human carries the expected ballot-bound signal and verifies both through Developer Portal and canonical historical verifier call\\.\\\\n\\\\n## SDD authority\\\\n`software-design/sdd\\.md` — `Gate 0-A: World v4 ballot binding`\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance evidence\\\\n- Sanitized RP context and untouched IDKit result\\\\n- Expected and returned signal hashes\\\\n- Portal verification result\\\\n- Historical call input/result\\\\n- Mutated signal/action/nonce/proof verdicts\\\\n- Machine-readable `GO \\| GO WITH CONSTRAINT \\| STOP \\| BLOCKED` report\\\\n\\\\n## External prerequisites\\\\nProduction World RP registration, Orb-verified participant, World App, archive RPC access\\.\\\\n\\\\n## Handoff\\\\nUse the standard Part III handoff comment before ending each working session\\.'\\);\nissue_b=\\$\\(gh issue create --repo \"\\$repo\" --title 'Gate 0-B: Establish World v4 Room uniqueness semantics' --label spike --label protocol --label world-id --label evidence --milestone \"\\$milestone\" --body \\$'## Outcome\\\\nProduction experiments establish whether one human can obtain more than one independently usable Room capability under the same RP/action\\.\\\\n\\\\n## SDD authority\\\\n`software-design/sdd\\.md` — `Gate 0-B: World v4 Room uniqueness`\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance evidence\\\\n- Same action/signal repeated with fresh RP context\\\\n- Same action with changed signal\\\\n- Different Room action\\\\n- Issuance/refusal behavior and nullifier observations\\\\n- Independent proof verification\\\\n- Machine-readable `GO \\| GO WITH CONSTRAINT \\| STOP \\| BLOCKED` report\\\\n\\\\n## Stop condition\\\\nIf fresh usable nullifiers can be generated for the same human/RP/action, stop capability implementation and revise Part I\\.\\\\n\\\\n## Handoff\\\\nUse the standard Part III handoff comment before ending each working session\\.'\\);\nissue_c=\\$\\(gh issue create --repo \"\\$repo\" --title 'Gate 0-C: Prove HashPack wallet-signed HCS chunking' --label spike --label hedera --label evidence --milestone \"\\$milestone\" --body \\$'## Outcome\\\\nA real HashPack account signs and pays for a complete multi-chunk HCS logical message on Hedera testnet, and Mirror REST reconstructs its public evidence\\.\\\\n\\\\n## SDD authority\\\\n`software-design/sdd\\.md` — `Gate 0-C: HashPack wallet-signed chunking`\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance evidence\\\\n- 1,023 / 1,024 / 1,025 byte submissions\\\\n- Real proof-envelope-size submission\\\\n- Approval count and partial rejection behavior\\\\n- Every transaction ID and receipt\\\\n- Raw Mirror responses with payer, initial transaction ID, chunk number/total, sequence and timestamp\\\\n- Machine-readable `GO \\| GO WITH CONSTRAINT \\| STOP \\| BLOCKED` report\\\\n\\\\n## Constraint\\\\nEach HCS chunk is capped at 1,024 bytes\\. Topic Submit support alone is not acceptance; complete real-device chunk behavior must be observed\\.\\\\n\\\\n## Handoff\\\\nUse the standard Part III handoff comment before ending each working session\\.'\\);\nissue_d=\\$\\(gh issue create --repo \"\\$repo\" --title 'Gate 0-D: Replay World proof at finalized historical state' --label spike --label world-id --label evidence --milestone \"\\$milestone\" --body \\$'## Outcome\\\\nTwo independent archive RPC paths reproduce the same World proof verdict at the same finalized World block and expose all verification-critical dependencies\\.\\\\n\\\\n## SDD authority\\\\n`software-design/sdd\\.md` — `Gate 0-D: World historical replay`\\\\n\\\\n## Acceptance evidence\\\\n- Block number/hash/timestamp and finalized observation\\\\n- Proxy implementation and dependency snapshot\\\\n- Provider capability and agreement report\\\\n- Valid proof call and altered-proof revert\\\\n- Unavailable/disagreement classification\\\\n- Machine-readable `GO \\| GO WITH CONSTRAINT \\| STOP \\| BLOCKED` report\\\\n\\\\n## Handoff\\\\nUse the standard Part III handoff comment before ending each working session\\.'\\);\nprintf '%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n%s\\\\n' \"\\$issue_a\" \"\\$issue_b\" \"\\$issue_c\" \"\\$issue_d\"$/": {
